\title{gambitR: Chess Engine, Analysis and Interactive Study Tools}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A self-contained chess toolkit in native R. Provides legal move generation, game-state tracking and 'FEN'/'PGN' parsing, position evaluation and a minimax search with alpha-beta pruning for play and simulation, batch tournament simulation between strategies, an opening explorer and puzzle trainer, and an interactive 'Shiny' application for playing, analysing, studying and annotating games. An optional 'UCI' engine hook enables deeper analysis when an external engine such as 'Stockfish' is available.
